# The dirty-page artifact, not fixture data.
#
# `rebuildIndex` and the multi-item write path both drop one of these into the
# content directory, so it lands in whatever fixture was being generated — and
# from F29 onward portfolio has a pagination index, so it lands here too. It
# carries a wall-clock `updatedAt`, so committing it means a spurious diff every
# time a fixture is regenerated, and nothing in this suite reads it. Recipe's
# fixture tree carries the identical rule for the identical reason; a real
# content repository ignores it via `initializeContentGit`.
.pagination-changes.json
